  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Seismic Activity Monitored By BMKG",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian meteorology agency, BMKG, is monitoring ongoing seismic activity including a magnitude 5.4 quake in Nias and tremors across NTT and Maluku.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "A magnitude 5.4 earthquake was recorded in Nias Barat, North Sumatra, with no tsunami threat reported.",
    "Earlier, a magnitude 5.8 earthquake impacted the Manggarai and Ngada regions, followed by multiple aftershocks.",
    "Authorities are also addressing recent seismic disturbances in Maluku and Intan Jaya, which caused some localized property damage."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian Agency for Meteorology, Climatology, and Geophysics (BMKG) is currently tracking a series of seismic events across various Indonesian provinces. A magnitude 5.4 earthquake recently occurred in Nias Barat, North Sumatra, on November 19, 2026, which officials confirmed carried no risk of a tsunami. This follows a period of heightened geological activity in the East Nusa Tenggara (NTT) region, where a magnitude 5.8 earthquake in the Manggarai and Ngada areas triggered at least 17 aftershocks within an hour. Experts have linked these NTT tremors to the Flores back-arc thrust. Additionally, earlier reports indicated significant seismic activity in Maluku Tenggara, involving a magnitude 7.1 earthquake that caused damage to local infrastructure, including a government-managed warehouse. The agency continues to monitor these regions to provide updates on potential risks and seismic patterns to the public.",
